Implement user story SKY-002-b: Test suite for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch (no real network calls). Tests must cover: URL/header construction, successful response parsing, HTTP error rejection, missing-key constructor errors, malformed response handling, and mock-mode behavior (MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns fixture without fetch; non-'true' values perform real fetch).

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach restoration — no real network calls in any test
- Test verifies searchFlights constructs the correct RapidAPI URL and includes the apiKey in request headers
- Test verifies a successful API response is parsed into a FlightResult[] matching the FlightResult interface shape
- Test verifies searchFlights rejects on HTTP 4xx/5xx with an Error that includes the status code in its message
- Test verifies SkyscannerClient constructor throws a descriptive Error when apiKey is missing or empty (including empty-string RAPIDAPI_KEY scenario)
- Test verifies searchFlights rejects with a parse/validation Error when the response body is malformed or missing expected fields
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' causes searchFlights to return deterministic fixture data (≥2 results, valid shape, varying prices) without invoking global fetch (fetch spy asserted never called)
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API with non-'true' values (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') results in a real fetch call; vitest run exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- SkyscannerClient class is exported from src/skyscanner/client.ts
- Constructor signature: constructor(options?: { apiKey?: string }) — options is optional object with optional apiKey property
- Constructor throws 'apiKey is required but was not provided and RAPIDAPI_KEY is unset' when both options.apiKey and process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY are undefined
- Constructor throws 'apiKey cannot be an empty string' when options.apiKey is empty string
- Constructor throws 'RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable cannot be an empty string' when process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY is empty string and options.apiKey is undefined
- Constructor-provided apiKey takes precedence over RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number; }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number; }
- searchFlights checks process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' (exact string match) before making network request
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true', searchFlights returns deterministic mock data from #getMockResults() without calling fetch
- Mock data returns exactly 3 FlightResult objects with varying prices: 299, 189, 450
- Mock data uses currency 'USD', airlines 'Mock Airlines', 'Budget Air', 'Premium Airways'
- Mock data has stops values 0, 1, 0 respectively
- When MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API !== 'true', searchFlights constructs URL: https://skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com/v3/flights/live/search/simple
- Query params appended to URL: 'origin', 'destination', 'date', and optionally 'adults' if provided
- Request headers include: 'X-RapidAPI-Key' with apiKey, 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner-api.p.rapidapi.com', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'
- searchFlights uses globalThis.fetch to make GET request
- On HTTP error (!response.ok), searchFlights throws Error with message 'HTTP error: ${response.status}'
- Response parsing validates data is non-null object, has 'data' property that is an array
- Response parsing validates each item has all 7 required fields: price, currency, airline, departure, arrival, duration, stops
- Response parsing validates price is number, currency is string, airline is string, departure is string, arrival is string, duration is number, stops is number
- Parse errors throw with specific messages: 'Response body is malformed: expected an object', 'Response body is missing expected field: data', 'Response body data field is not an array', 'Response body data[${i}] is not an object', 'Response body data[${i}] is missing expected field: ${field}', 'Response body data[${i}].${field} is not a ${type}'
- No validation exists for adults parameter being 0 or negative — adults=0 is valid
- No validation exists for empty string origin/destination/date — empty strings are passed through
- No validation exists for date format — any string is accepted
- No validation exists for IATA code format — any string is accepted for origin/destination

